# The turn engine's own lines (Docs/Design/84 §8.2-8.4, Phase 3). Each is a move line: a rule with no concept, found by
# the move it makes (`does`), so it answers in any talk where its criteria hold. Their words are the speaker's dialect
# through the grammar's symbols (#farewell#, #greet#, #agree#...): Coldwater's "Fair winds", Saltwell's "Go in peace".
# Phase 8 writes the bulk of the shared lines; these are what a talk needs to open properly, to close, and to answer
# something owed when nothing written for it holds (the fallbacks walk down to ack).
#
# They are said often, by anyone, so they are short (under six words: never a "distinctive" line heard again or said by
# two in one place, R4 and R5), and they are spread wide: few criteria (a rule whose criteria hold outscores the rest
# and would be said most of the time), many alternatives.

## Closing (§8.4, after Schegloff and Sacks): the farewell pair, with a preclose and its answer before it when the talk
## has run long enough and its budget has room (its frames' preclose makes the room smaller). The one at work closes
## first, else the one who didn't speak last. A line may preclose and take leave at once.

rule cv_pre_any
does preclose
say Well. There it is. | Right, then. | Anyway. | Ah, well. | Well, that's that.

rule cv_pre_any2
does preclose
say I mustn't keep you. | Still. Can't stand about. | Well. Enough of me. | So. There we are.

rule cv_pre_work
does preclose
when self.working=yes
say Back to it, then. | Work won't wait. | I'd better get on. | This won't earn my keep. | Well. Hands to it.

rule cv_accept_any
does accept_preclose
say Go on, then. | Right you are. | You do that. | Off you go. | Aye, I'd best too.

rule cv_accept_any2
does accept_preclose
say #agree#. | And me. | Right. | Aye, go on. | Same here.

rule cv_bye_any
does farewell
say #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#. | #farewell#, then. | Take care.

rule cv_bye_any2
does farewell
say Be seeing you. | Till next time. | #later.capitalize#, then. | Look after yourself.

rule cv_bye_any3
does farewell
say Mind yourself. | Go well. | I'll see you. | See you about.

rule cv_bye_both
does preclose farewell
say Well. #farewell#. | Right. #farewell#. | Anyway. Take care. | Well. I'll see you.

rule cv_bye_both2
does preclose farewell
say Off I go, then. | I'll let you be. | Right. Till next time. | I'll leave you to it.

rule cv_bye_night
does farewell
when here.time=night|dusk
say Good night. | Sleep sound. | Good night, #address#. | Rest well. | Mind the dark. | Don't stay up late.

rule cv_bye_young
does farewell
when self.stage=young|adolescent
say Bye! | See you! | Bye, then!

rule cv_return_any
does farewell.return
say #farewell#. | And you. | You too. | #farewell#, #address#.

rule cv_return_any2
does farewell.return
say Take care, now. | Mind how you go. | Aye. #farewell#. | Till next time.

rule cv_return_any3
does farewell.return
say Go on, then. | Right you are. | #later.capitalize#. | Aye, you too.

rule cv_return_any4
does farewell.return
say And you, #address#. | Mind yourself. | Go well. | See you.

rule cv_return_night
does farewell.return
when here.time=night|dusk
say Good night. | Sleep well. | Sleep sound. | Rest well. | Good night, #address#. | And you. Mind the dark.

rule cv_return_young
does farewell.return
when self.stage=young|adolescent
say Bye! | Bye, then! | See you!

## Opening (§8.4): strangers greet properly; a host greets a guest. Kin and housemates skip the greeting. A greeting is
## said in the same breath as an opener that says what it does and doesn't open itself.

rule cv_greet_strangers
does greet
when pair.band=strangers
say #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.

rule cv_greet_host
does greet
when here.place=tavern self.job=innkeeper
say #greet#. Sit yourself down. | #greet#. Take the warm end.

rule cv_greet_back
does greet.return
say #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.

## Answers owed when nothing written for them holds (§7.2's fallbacks, walked down to ack). Plain, and true whatever
## came before them.

rule cv_ack_any
does ack
say I see. | Is that so. | Well, well. | So it goes.

rule cv_ack_any2
does ack
say Fancy that. | I'll bear it in mind. | There it is. | Well, now.

rule cv_agree_any
does agree
say #agree#. | Can't argue with that. | That's the truth of it.

rule cv_accept_apology
does accept_apology
say No harm done. | Think nothing of it. | It's forgotten.

rule cv_deflect_thanks
does deflect_thanks
say Any time. | Don't mention it. | It's nothing.

rule cv_accept_decline
does accept_decline
say Another time, then. | Fair enough. | No matter.
